      "filename": "Beijing, Tiananmen Square (6169820273).jpg",
      "title": "File:Beijing, Tiananmen Square (6169820273).jpg",
      "url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/d1/Beijing%2C_Tiananmen_Square_%286169820273%29.jpg",
      "descriptionUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Beijing,_Tiananmen_Square_(6169820273).jpg",
      "width": 1776,
      "height": 1164,
      "mime": "image/jpeg",
      "license": "CC BY 2.0",
      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0",
      "artist": "Arian Zwegers",
      "description": "Beijing, Tiananmen Square, Monument to the People's Heroes and the Mao Zedong Mausoleum\nTiananmen Square is a large city square in the center of Beijing, China, named after the Tiananmen Gate (Gate of Heavenly Peace) located to its North, separating it from the Forbidden City. Tiananmen Square is the third largest city square in the world (440,000 m² - 880m by 500m). It has great cultural significance as it was the site of several important events in Chinese history. Outside China, the square is best known in recent memory as the focal point of the Tiananmen Square protests of 1989, a pro-democracy movement which ended on 4 June 1989 with the declaration of martial law in Beijing by the government and the death of at least hundreds of protesters.\nThe Monument to the People's Heroes is a ten-story obelisk that was erected as a national monument of the People's Republic of China. The Monument was built in memory of the martyrs who laid down their lives for the revolutionary struggles of the Chinese people during the 19th and 20th centuries.\nThe Chairman Mao Memorial Hall, commonly known as the Mausoleum of Mao Zedong, or the Mao Mausoleum, is the final resting place of Mao Zedong, Chairman of the Politburo of the Communist Party of China from 1943 and the chairman of the Central Committee of the Communist Party of China from 1945 until his death in 1976.\n\n(From Wikipedia, en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tiananmen_Square, en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Monument_to_the_People%27s_Heroes, en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mausoleum_of_Mao_Zedong)",
      "dateCreated": "1995-05-13 13:24",
